ge packets/outputs on disk, read back only digests) and mandatory dissent preservation. Companion `deliberative-analysis` skill handles solo anti-overconfidence with escalation into the arena. [VERIFIED]\n385-- **GNOSIS takeaway:** Adopt the escalation-trigger checklist plus the \"dissent preserved in the synthesis artifact\" contract as the standard shape of independent-review evidence, and its disk-staged packet discipline for keeping arena rounds out of the orchestrator's context.\n386-\n387-### TwinRouterBench — Two-track benchmark (static labels + live SWE-bench) for routing each agent step to the cheapest sufficient LLM\n388-\n389-- **Identity:** https://github.com/CommonstackAI/TwinRouterBench @ 7cbb0de (2026-08-18) | Apache-2.0 (standard 202-line text incl. appendix, no NOTICE, no riders — VERIFIED) | Python ≥3.10, JSONL datasets, JSON configs\n390-- **Risk:** MEDIUM — reading it is safe, but reproducing the dynamic track executes a live agent loop (`swerouter/harness/container_runner.py`, containers) against paid APIs and auto-loads `.env` from the package directory (README \"Where to run commands\") — real spend and credential-handling surface if ever run. Static track has a keyless `--backend mock` mode. [VERIFIED]\n391-- **Decision:** BENCHMARK_AGAINST — when GNOSIS implements per-step model routing, use its static question bank and downgrade-search labeling protocol as the external baseline rather than inventing a homegrown eval.\n392-- **Key mechanism:** `twinrouterbench/` CLI exposes four surfaces (`data` / `static` / `dynamic` / `swe`). The static track builds \"cheapest sufficient tier\" labels per routed step via downgrade search with mixed-model execution verification (970 labels, 520 trajectories, 5 workloads); the dynamic track routes every live call of a mini-SWE-agent across 100 held-out SWE-bench Verified cases, measuring end-to-end resolution vs realized API spend. The framing insight: routers must decide \"which model handles the next call given the full current prefix,\" not one model per whole prompt. Headline: trained router 75/100 at $25.66 vs all-Opus 74/100 at $54.73 (53.1% cost cut). [Structure VERIFIED; headline numbers SELF-REPORTED]\n393-- **GNOSIS takeaway:** Per-step cheapest-sufficient routing with prefix-conditioned decisions is the right cost-control model for GNOSIS's multi-agent loops, and its downgrade-search labeling is a reusable method for generating routing ground truth from GNOSIS's own task traces.\n394-\n395-### symphony — OpenAI's spec + reference daemon that turns tracker issues into isolated autonomous coding-agent runs\n396-\n397-- **Identity:** https://github.com/openai/symphony @ 8001b52 | Apache-2.0 (LICENSE verified verbatim, standard text, no riders; NOTICE = plain Apache boilerplate, Copyright 2025 OpenAI) | Elixir (reference impl in `elixir/`), language-agnostic Markdown spec\ntests\\test_convergence.py:7:    ConvergenceLoop,\ntests\\test_convergence.py:9:    ConvergencePolicy,\ntests\\test_convergence.py:16:    git_fingerprint,\ntests\\test_convergence.py:72:def _run(script: _Script, policy: ConvergencePolicy | None = None):\ntests\\test_convergence.py:73:    loop = ConvergenceLoop(\ntests\\test_convergence.py:74:        policy or ConvergencePolicy(max_rounds=10, max_unchanged_rounds=3),\ntests\\test_convergence.py:81:class TestConvergenceLoop(unittest.TestCase):\ntests\\test_convergence.py:158:        result = _run(script, ConvergencePolicy(max_rounds=6, max_unchanged_rounds=3))\ntests\\test_convergence.py:172:        result = _run(script, ConvergencePolicy(max_rounds=6, max_unchanged_rounds=3))\ntests\\test_convergence.py:185:        result = _run(script, ConvergencePolicy(max_rounds=3, max_unchanged_rounds=99))\ntests\\test_convergence.py:221:        result = _run(script, ConvergencePolicy(max_rounds=3, max_unchanged_rounds=99))\ntests\\test_convergence.py:262:        loop = ConvergenceLoop(\ntests\\test_convergence.py:263:            ConvergencePolicy(max_round