{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"findings\":[{\"title\":\"Evidence-collection failures still advance the stalemate streak\",\"file\":\"src/gnosis/kernel/convergence.py\",\"line\":244,\"severity\":\"major\",\"claim\":\"The loop can return STALEMATE after verification or review evidence collection failed, contrary to the requirement that such rounds never count toward stalemate.\",\"scenario\":\"Use one stable fingerprint and make verify_fn or review_fn raise for max_unchanged_rounds consecutive rounds. fingerprint remains non-None, so unchanged increments at lines 244-251 even though evidence_ok is false; lines 321-323 then return STALEMATE.\"},{\"title\":\"Fingerprint gaps do not break an unchanged-fingerprint streak\",\"file\":\"src/gnosis/kernel/convergence.py\",\"line\":244,\"severity\":\"major\",\"claim\":\"A later recurring fingerprint is treated as consecutive unchanged state across rounds where the fingerprint was unavailable.\",\"scenario\":\"Return fingerprints A, None, A, A with max_unchanged_rounds=2. The final two usable A values advance the retained streak to 2 and yield STALEMATE, although the intervening gap means the kernel has no evidence that the repository did not change and revert. tests/test_convergence.py:164-176 codifies this unsafe behavior by expecting the stale baseline to survive four unavailable rounds.\"},{\"title\":\"An unchanged DONE claim can still immediately produce CONVERGED\",\"file\":\"src/gnosis/kernel/convergence.py\",\"line\":309,\"severity\":\"major\",\"claim\":\"The advertised signal-without-evidence downgrade is only a warning; it does not prevent the same unchanged state from closing the task.\",\"scenario\":\"In round 1, verification fails and the fixer returns FixReport(claims_done=True) without changing fingerprint A. In round 2, a flaky or gameable verifier returns passed and the reviewer returns PASS while fingerprint remains A. The loop records the warning at lines 232-